<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Burney returns two weeks after presenting with a right breast lump and a year of heavy, dull breast ache. The diagnostic mammogram and ultrasound twelve days ago showed a 2.4 cm spiculated mass at 10 o&apos;clock in the right breast, BI-RADS 5, with normal axillary nodes and dense breast tissue. The ultrasound-guided core biopsy ten days ago shows invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, strongly estrogen and progesterone receptor positive and HER2 negative. The ache is unchanged and does not wake her. She has no bone pain, cough, headaches, abdominal pain, or weight loss. She saw Dr. Marsh of breast surgery this morning. She is frightened of an operation and has asked that every step be explained beforehand and that she be warned before anything is done; with that, she feels able to go ahead. She has no family history of breast or ovarian cancer that she knows of, but her mother died when she was ten and little is known of her mother&apos;s family. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Imaging BI-RADS 5; core biopsy invasive ductal carcinoma, ER and PR positive, HER2 negative</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Unchanged dull ache; no symptoms of spread</td></tr><tr><td>Coordination</td><td>Breast surgery seen this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Family history</td><td>Limited: mother died when she was ten</td></tr><tr><td>Concerns</td><td>Fear of surgery; wants each step explained and to be warned in advance</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

