    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast, clinical stage T2 N0 (cT2 cN0 M0), hormone receptor positive, HER2 negative (C50.411)</content>. Early breast cancer. With no symptoms of spread and a clinical stage of T2 N0, staging scans and tumor markers are not indicated. Because the breasts are dense, Dr. Marsh advises MRI before choosing between breast-conserving surgery and mastectomy. [S]<list><item>Bilateral breast MRI in four days, as Dr. Marsh advised.</item><item>Germline multigene panel test sent today, before surgery, as recommended for breast cancer at 65 or younger.</item><item>Surgery date to be set after the MRI and the genetic result; pre-anesthesia clinic visit to be booked.</item><item>She will be told in advance of every procedure, as she asked.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Estrogen receptor positive status (Z17.0)</content>. ER 95 percent and PR 70 percent: she will benefit from endocrine therapy after surgery. [S]<list><item>Recurrence score on the surgical specimen to decide whether chemotherapy would add benefit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Diagnostic mammography and ultrasound of the breast and axilla</td><td>At presentation with a palpable mass</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done twelve days ago: 2.4 cm spiculated mass, BI-RADS 5; normal axillary nodes; dense breasts</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Core biopsy with ER, PR, and HER2 testing</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2; ER 95 percent, PR 70 percent, HER2 1+ (negative), Ki-67 15 percent</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Breast MRI for extent of disease</td><td>Optional at diagnosis; considered for dense breasts or when surgical planning is uncertain</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked in four days</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT, bone scan, or PET for distant spread</td><td>Only with symptoms or clinical stage III</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Clinical stage T2 N0 with no symptoms of spread</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Tumor markers (CEA, CA 15-3, CA 27.29)</td><td>Not recommended for early breast cancer</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Germline genetic testing</td><td>At diagnosis, for breast cancer at 65 or younger</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Multigene panel sample sent today; result expected in about three weeks, before surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress, depression, and anxiety screen (PHQ-9 and GAD-7)</td><td>At diagnosis and at periodic intervals</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 5 and GAD-7 7, mild; supported today and offered the cancer center&apos;s counseling service</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lymphedema baseline arm measurements</td><td>Before axillary surgery</td><td>Due</td><td>To be measured at the pre-anesthesia visit before surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Breast surgery</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen this morning; recommendations in the consultation note</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Medical oncology</td><td>After surgery, with the surgical pathology</td><td>Due</td><td>To review the pathology and recurrence score after surgery</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Pre-anesthesia evaluation</td><td>Before surgery</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Pre-anesthesia clinic visit to be booked once the date is set</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Activity and preparation for surgery</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking 30 minutes a day; never smoker; shoulder exercise leaflet given</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Complete diagnosis, staging, and surgery within eight weeks of presentation. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Surgery under anesthesia with pain controlled without opioids after discharge. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Start adjuvant endocrine therapy with a bone-health plan. In progress; target 2026-10-19 [S]</item><item>Regain full right shoulder movement and keep lymphedema risk low. In progress; target 2026-10-29 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Germline Testing in Patients With Breast Cancer: ASCO-Society of Surgical Oncology Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2024 (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Breast MRI in four days. Genetic result in about three weeks. Surgery date from the breast surgery team. Primary care review about three weeks after surgery. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: review three weeks after right mastectomy; start of endocrine therapy and survivorship care. [S]</paragraph></text>

